# One pass

- Start with the `apps/api` composition root, the `packages/axc/rest` and `packages/axc/application-services` entries and nearest existing feature, and the `packages/axc-verification` acceptance entry. Use one batched search to identify them, then read them in parallel.
- Use at most one follow-up read batch to resolve a specific unknown. A failed check permits the reads needed to fix it.
- Do not reopen a file or successful command, summarize intermediate work, or start a second exploration, review pass, or subagent.
- Write each new file once. Make a follow-up edit only to resolve a specific unknown or failed check.
- Format changed files once with `pnpm exec biome check --write --no-errors-on-unmatched <paths>`.
- Run one affected-package check through `node scripts/agent-check.mjs -- <command>`. That command includes the affected package test and `pnpm run knip`.
- Run `pnpm run verify` once through the same wrapper as the final gate.
- On failure, fix the reported cause, rerun only the failed package through the wrapper, then run wrapped `pnpm run verify` once more.
- Ponytail and Caveman apply in full. This rule limits tool calls only.

## Command output

- Trust the wrapper's `PASS` result. Do not inspect its successful log.
- On failure, use its first error block. Read more of the temporary log only when that block cannot identify the cause.
- Final reply: changes, commands, pass or fail, limitations, dependency justification, and security findings. Do not narrate the work.
